From 336ef878b703dfb0301dacea6341ccbc00054f6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fernando Luiz Cola <fernando.luiz@pantacor.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:28:06 -0300
Subject: [RFC PATCH 7/8] busybox: add a Pantavisor-only patch series

Pantavisor needs six busybox changes, all from its busybox-pv fork
(github.com/pantavisor/busybox-pv), rebased onto 1.38.0:

 - nsenter: --caps to adopt the target's capabilities, and -C/--cgroup
 - mdev: FOLLOW_X_ROOT and MDEV_CONF, so an mdev daemon can serve the
   /dev of a container root and follow its pivot root
 - netlink: do not bind with a pid that may not be unique
 - mdev: MODALIAS support, loading PCI drivers during 'mdev -s', and a
   fix for the segfault it caused with name rules in mdev.conf

The MODALIAS scan has no Kconfig switch and would change 'mdev -s' for
everyone, and the rest only matters to Pantavisor. So the patches go
into series.pantavisor, next to the unchanged series, and a hidden
BUSYBOX_SERIES picks it when PANTAVISOR is enabled. PTXdist already
reads <PKG>_SERIES for every package; this is the first user besides
the kernel. Builds without Pantavisor apply the same patches as before.

BUSYBOX_FEATURE_MDEV_FOLLOW_X_ROOT goes into rules/busybox.in, as
config/busybox mirrors stock busybox's Kconfig.

Signed-off-by: Fernando Luiz Cola <fernando.luiz@pantacor.com>
